[2025-07-10T09:34:26.366Z] [OUT] {"id":"1752140066366-1cw4w8scn","timestamp":"2025-07-10T09:34:26.366Z","type":"assistant.action","data":{"phaseId":"phase-2","action":"thinking","content":"Let me think through this step by step:\n\n1. **Logical groupings of schemas needed:**\n   - Based on my analysis, I need to create schemas for FHIR resources. The main structure is:\n     - FHIR Bundle (top-level container)\n     - Individual FHIR Resources (Patient, Observation, Encounter, etc.)\n     - Common FHIR data types (CodeableConcept, Quantity, Period, etc.)\n\n2. **Schema organization:**\n   - I should create a hierarchy:\n     - `fhir-bundle.ts` - Main bundle schema\n     - `fhir-resources.ts` - Individual resource schemas\n     - `fhir-datatypes.ts` - Common FHIR data types\n     - `index.ts` - Export everything\n\n3. **From my analysis, I know:**\n   - All files are FHIR Bundles with resourceType \"Bundle\" and type \"transaction\"\n   - Each bundle has an array of entries\n   - Each entry has a resource field\n   - Resources have different types: Patient, Observation, Encounter, etc.\n   - Common patterns like codes, quantities, periods, etc.\n\nLet me start by examining the actual data structure more carefully to build accurate schemas."}}
