ion needs high-precision decimal handling\n * - Race/ethnicity coding follows federal OMB standards\n */\nexport const Extension = z.object({\n  url: FhirString.describe('Extension identifier - full URI or relative path (CRITICAL: not FhirUri due to relative URLs)'),\n  valueString: FhirString.optional().describe('String value - used for names, race/ethnicity text'),\n  valueBoolean: FhirBoolean.optional().describe('Boolean value - rarely used in this dataset'),\n  valueDecimal: FhirDecimal.optional().describe('Decimal value - high-precision coordinates (42.2862619550264)'),\n  valueCode: FhirCode.optional().describe('Code value - rarely used in this dataset'),\n  valueCoding: Coding.optional().describe('Coding value - OMB race/ethnicity codes'),\n  valueCodeableConcept: CodeableConcept.optional().describe('CodeableConcept value - rarely used'),\n  valueQuantity: Quantity.optional().describe('Quantity value - not used in this dataset'),\n  valueDateTime: FhirDateTime.optional().describe('DateTime value - not used in this dataset'),\n  valueDate: FhirDate.optional().describe('Date value - not used in this dataset'),\n  extension: z.array(z.lazy(() => Extension)).optional().describe('Nested extensions - common for demographics and geolocation')\n}).describe('FHIR extension - supports relative URLs, demographics, and geolocation patterns');"}}}
